r in the center is a good strategy to start.\n\nTherefore, my final recommendation is to choose C3 (column C, row 3).\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The move (C, 3) is the most strategically sound option available. It is the only move located within the central 4x4 zone (rows 3-6, columns C-F), which is critical for maintaining control and piece grouping in the opening.\n\nReason: By playing (C, 3), you flip two opponent pieces (C4, C5) to create a solid, central block of your own pieces. This move minimizes the "frontier" (the number of empty squares adjacent to your pieces), limiting the opponent\'s mobility and forcing them to play towards the outer edges (B-row or G-row), which is generally disadvantageous for them. Other options like F7 are dangerous (risking corner access), and moves on the B or G rows expand the game to the outer shell prematurely.\n\nAnswer: (C, 3)'}
